1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,038
A transactional outbox stores a business change and an event record in

2
00:00:04,038 --> 00:00:05,384
the same local transaction.

3
00:00:05,534 --> 00:00:08,109
A relay later publishes the event to a broker.

4
00:00:08,259 --> 00:00:12,567
This closes the loss window where a database commit succeeds but event

5
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:13,644
publication never happens.

6
00:00:13,794 --> 00:00:18,715
It does not eliminate duplicates: a relay may publish successfully and crash

7
00:00:18,715 --> 00:00:19,945
before recording completion.

8
00:00:20,095 --> 00:00:23,009
Consumers must make duplicate delivery safe.

9
00:00:23,159 --> 00:00:27,109
Store the event ID and local effect in one transaction where possible.

10
00:00:27,259 --> 00:00:32,382
Partition ordering applies within the broker’s ordering boundary, not globally across all

11
00:00:32,382 --> 00:00:32,809
messages.

12
00:00:32,959 --> 00:00:37,613
Design event schemas for compatibility and keep event payloads focused on stable

13
00:00:37,613 --> 00:00:38,388
business facts.

14
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:43,239
OrderTransactions.complete changes a pending order to CONFIRMED or REJECTED and inserts an

15
00:00:43,239 --> 00:00:45,589
outbox event in the same transaction.

16
00:00:45,739 --> 00:00:48,475
Repeating completion does not add a second event.

17
00:00:48,625 --> 00:00:53,047
The supplied project stores the outbox but does not ship a broker

18
00:00:53,047 --> 00:00:57,101
relay; implementing and crash-testing that relay is the advanced messaging exercise.

19
00:00:57,251 --> 00:01:00,917
Implement a relay with bounded batches and a deduplicating consumer.

20
00:01:01,067 --> 00:01:04,756
Inject a crash after publish but before acknowledgement storage.

21
00:01:04,906 --> 00:01:09,138
Restart and demonstrate that the event may repeat while the consumer’s business

22
00:01:09,138 --> 00:01:10,196
effect remains single.

23
00:01:10,346 --> 00:01:13,903
Use stable event IDs and durable consumer deduplication.

24
00:01:14,053 --> 00:01:19,821
If the consumer calls an external provider, local deduplication alone is insufficient;

25
00:01:19,821 --> 00:01:22,224
use provider idempotency and reconciliation.

26
00:01:22,374 --> 00:01:26,610
State the exact effect and failure model before using the phrase exactly

27
00:01:26,610 --> 00:01:26,963
once.

28
00:01:27,113 --> 00:01:27,784
Question.

29
00:01:27,934 --> 00:01:29,818
What does the outbox guarantee?

30
00:01:29,968 --> 00:01:30,544
Answer.

31
00:01:30,694 --> 00:01:35,651
The local business change and event record commit together, assuming the database

32
00:01:35,651 --> 00:01:36,477
transaction succeeds.

33
00:01:36,627 --> 00:01:37,298
Question.

34
00:01:37,448 --> 00:01:39,587
Why can outbox delivery repeat?

35
00:01:39,737 --> 00:01:40,313
Answer.

36
00:01:40,463 --> 00:01:45,363
Publishing and recording relay progress are separate operations, leaving a crash window.
